cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use WfLedger in research, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "WfLedger: a discrete-event simulator for scientific workflow scheduling research"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "He"
    given-names: "Yixin"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-27"
license: "GPL-3.0-or-later"
repository-code: "https://github.com/yixin0724/wfledger"
url: "https://github.com/yixin0724/wfledger"
abstract: >-
  A discrete-event simulator for research on scientific workflow scheduling. It runs
  static planners and online schedulers from the literature under one declared model
  of workflows, platforms, storage, networks, energy and failures, and compares them
  with paired statistics across workflow instances. Runs can optionally keep a full
  evidence record that is re-runnable and independently checkable.
keywords:
  - scientific workflows
  - workflow scheduling
  - discrete-event simulation
  - reproducibility
  - energy-aware scheduling
  - cloud computing
